stateDiagram-v2
    %% CURRENT controller session state; no DB status FK.
    state "init" as init
    state "email_created" as email_created
    state "email_verified" as email_verified
    [*] --> init
    init --> email_created: progress_email_flow!(:create)
    init --> email_verified: progress_email_flow!(:update)
    init --> init: reset_email_flow!
    email_created --> email_created: progress_email_flow!(:create)
    email_created --> email_verified: progress_email_flow!(:update)
    email_created --> init: reset_email_flow!
    email_verified --> email_created: progress_email_flow!(:create)
    email_verified --> email_verified: progress_email_flow!(:update)
    email_verified --> init: reset_email_flow!
    init --> init: progress_email_flow!(:destroy) declared helper
    email_created --> init: progress_email_flow!(:destroy) declared helper
    email_verified --> init: progress_email_flow!(:destroy) declared helper
    note right of init
        Missing or invalid session values normalize to init.
        Helper writes do not check the prior state.
        HTTP entry guards and OTP verification narrow callers.
        No persisted expiry or cancel value; reset is the escape.
    end note
